//- built once by srcbuild into static/static.html, then served by
//- express.static - there is no request and no `settings` here. that is
//- deliberate: `domain` and `sysinfo` belong to the running server, and baking
//- them into a static file mixes dev and production domains and pins a version
//- that goes stale on the next deploy. see the view engine setup in
//- backend/engine/index.ls, where pug locals are left empty for this reason.
//- compare with view.pug, which renders per request at /demo/view and does get them.
doctype html
html
  head
  body
    h1 hi static page.
    div this page is built at build time, not rendered per request.
